          "snippet": "Optical tweezers are the perfect nano-tool for single-molecule manipulation and investigations [1]. With a correctly chosen wavelength they are nearly non-invasive and can be used to manipulate entire living microorganisms [2,3] or track organelles inside a cell [4]. For single-molecule investigations, often a handle, for example in the form of a dielectric micronsized object, is attached to the molecule of interest.",
