        "Allan variances were calculated with a custom-made Matlab program [22]. We measured Allan variances for various objects and parameters (trap stiffness, acquisition frequency, piezo) by acquiring three time series. Then the parameter was altered and we repeated the measurements. If not stated otherwise, we plotted the overlapping Allan variance in a loglog plot.",
        "The maximum of the Allan variance is at πτ c where\n\nFor measurement intervals where the Allan variance is larger than the thermal limit, the data points are not correlated. The observation that the Allan variance is very close to the thermal limit in the measurement time span between 100 ms and 1 s is evidence of an extremely stable setup. The Allan variance has a global minimum at around 1-10 s, the exact postion of this minimum is dependent on the trap stiffness."
